<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2016/Hillside.jpg" alt="Plein air sketch of a hillside at Discovery Park" width="550" height="393" data-filename="Hillside.JPG" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Hillside. 5x7, oil on linen panel. 2016</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This sketch is based on a notan study that was done on location. Painting with some separation from the spring greens allows me to be much more creative with the color choices.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This isn't the first time in 17 days that a sketch didn't survive the morning after. There are a couple of passages in it that might be useful, but nothing that I haven't painted before. I thought the composition was weak, so I scraped everything off and used the panel for something else.</p>